      "dom_id": "question-67199",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Express the following arithmetic series using sigma notation.\n\n$$\n-12-7-2+3+8+…+28+33\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The first term ${a}_{1}=-12$ and the common difference is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =-7-(-12) \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the formula for the $n$th term is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-12+(n-1)(5) \\\\  & =-12+5n-5 \\\\  & =5n-17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe don't know the index of the last term, but we can find it using the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =33 \\\\ 5n-17 & =33 \\\\ 5n & =33+17 \\\\ 5n & =50 \\\\ n & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are $10$ terms in total, from $n=1$ to $n=10.$ So, the sigma notation for the given sum is:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{10}(5n-17)\n$$",
